# Set up editors

**Prerequisites:** [Install](/docs/start/install/) so Cargo can build the language server.
**You will do:** load the first-party extension and point it at a built server.
**Verify:** opening a `.rocci` file shows diagnostics and semantic highlighting.
**Next:** [Develop and inspect](/docs/how-to/develop-and-inspect/).

Editor support is **current** in this repository. There is no Marketplace /
extension-store install path yet. Build from the checkout.

The server binary is `rocci-language-server` (`cargo build -p rocci-rocdown-lsp`).
The VS Code and Zed extensions are thin LSP clients.

## VS Code

```sh
cargo build -p rocci-rocdown-lsp
uv run rocci-ops package vscode
code --install-extension editors/vscode/rocci-*.vsix
```

For a debug session, press **F5** in `editors/vscode` after building the server.
Setting `rocci.lsp.serverPath` overrides the packaged or `target/debug` binary.

Do not treat the README completion list as a language contract: `@on` and
role-first headers are **removed**. Author `@method:role(path)`.

## Zed

```sh
cargo build -p rocci-rocdown-lsp
```

In Zed, **zed: install dev extension** and choose `editors/zed`. Zed does not
bundle the server WASM. Lookup order: `lsp.rocci-language-server.binary.path`,
then `PATH`, then `{worktree}/target/debug/rocci-language-server`.

Enable semantic tokens for the Rocci language. File icons are an optional
**Rocci** icon theme in the same extension.

**Related:** `editors/vscode/README.md`, `editors/zed/README.md`.
